:Error Return Codes

     Foò  eacè oæ thå routineó iî thió seô oæ  byte-orienteä 
filå  I/Ï routines¬  thå Zerï Flaç anä thå Á Registeò plaù á 
keù rolå iî indicatinç thå erroò conditionó oæ thå routines.

     Iæ  thå Zerï Flaç ió Seô (Z© afteò á routinå  haó  beeî 
executed¬  theî  thió indicateó thaô nï erroò haó  occurred®  
Thå  Á  Registeò  ió eitheò unaffecteä (iî  mosô  cases©  oò 
containó  á  returneä valuå (iæ sï indicated¬  aó iî  Fn$GEÔ 
routines).

     Iæ thå Zerï Flaç ió Cleaò (NZ© afteò á routinå haó beeî 
executed¬  theî  thió indicateó thaô aî erroò haó  occurred®  
Thå Á Registeò no÷ containó thå Erroò Code®   Thå  followinç 
tablå  summarizeó  thå Erroò Codeó whicè maù bå returneä  iî 
thå Á Register.

     Thå  followinç  screeî  displaù  summarizeó  thå  Erroò 
Codes.


                   Summary of Error Codes
        Returned by Byte-Oriented File I/O Routines

          Code Meaning
          ---- -------

            1  GET or PUT attempted on an unopened file
            2  Disk Full (Ran out of space)
            3  Input File Not Found
            4  Attempt to Read Past EOF
            5  Directory Full
            6  Error in Closing a File
            7  Attempt to Open a File which is already Open

:Byte-Oriented File I/O Routines with Variable Buffers
     Iî additioî tï thå routineó mentioneä previously¬ á seô 
oæ byte-orienteä filå I/Ï routineó ió availablå undeò SYSLIÂ 
³  whicè permitó thå useò tï definå thå sizå anä locatioî oæ 
thå  bufferó tï bå used®   Thå routineó mentioneä abovå  alì 
uså 128-bytå buffers¬  and¬  oî largeò capacitù disë systemó 
(anä oî anù systemó iî general)¬ iô maù bå morå efficienô tï 
buffeò morå thaî 12¸ byteó aô á time®  Thió wilì cuô dowî oî 
thå  disë  activitù anä leavå morå  memory-baseä  processinç 
overhead.

     The routines described in this section are:

          Routine   Similar to  Function
          -------   ----------  --------
          FXI$OPEN  FIn$OPEN    Open File for Input
          FXO$OPEN  FOn$OPEN    Open File for Output
          FXI$CLOSE FIn$CLOSE   Close Input File
          FXO$CLOSE FOn$CLOSE   Close Output File
          FX$GET    Fn$GET      Get Byte
          FX$PUT    Fn$PUT      Put Byte
     Alì  oæ thå Filå Extendeä Bytå I/Ï Routineó  (FØ  meanó 
Filå  Extended©  worë  witè aî I/Ï Controì  Blocë  whicè  ió 
structured as follows:

Block     Length    User-
Offset    (Bytes)   Set?*     Function
------    -------   -----     --------
   0         1        Y       Number of 128-Byte Pages in
                                   Working Buffer
   1         1        N       End of File Flag
   2         2        N       Byte Counter
   4         2        N       Next Byte Pointer
   6         2        Y       Address of Working Buffer
   8        36        Y       FCB of File (Only FN and FT
                                   Fields Set by User)


ª  Bù  "User-Set"¬   É  meaî  thaô  thå  programmeò  haó  tï 
initializå thió valuå beforå theså routineó arå called.

     Thå  followinç  DB/DÓ  structurå  caî bå  useä  iî  thå 
calling program to implement the I/O Control Block:

     IOCTL:
               DB   8    ; Use 8 128-Byte Pages (1K)
               DS   1    ; Filled in by FXIO
               DS   2    ; Filled in by FXIO
               DS   2    ; Filled in by FXIO
               DW   WORK ; Address of Working Buffer
     IOCFCB:
               DS   1    ; Filled in by FXIO to 0
               DB   'MYFILE  '     ; File Name
               DB   'TXT'          ; File Type
               DS   24   ; Filled in by FXIO
     WORK:
               DS   128*8     ; Working Buffer (1K)

     Alì  oæ  thå FXIÏ routineó arå consistenô  iî  thaô  DÅ 
alwayó  pointó tï thå I/Ï Controì Blocë (IOCTÌ above© anä  Á 
anä  thå  PS× arå useä tï pasó flagó anä values®   Á  samplå 
program body which illustrates the calling procedures:

          ...
   ¼ Iniô IOCTL± anä IOCTL2¬ wherå ± ió input¬ ² ió output>
          ...
          LXI  D,IOCTL1
          CALL FXI$OPEN  ; Open 1 for Input
          JZ   FNF       ; File Not Found Error
          LXI  D,IOCTL2
          CALL FXO$OPEN  ; Open 2 for Output
          JZ   NODIR     ; No Dir Space Error
          ...


          ...
          LXI  D,IOCTL1
          CALL FX$GET    ; Get Next Input Byte in A
          JZ   EOF       ; Process EOF
          ...
          LXI  D,IOCTL2
          CALL FX$PUT    ; Put Byte in A to Output File
          JZ   WERR      ; Process Write Error
          ...
          LXI  D,IOCTL1
          CALL FXI$CLOSE ; Close Input File
          JZ   FCERR     ; File Close Error
          LXI  D,IOCTL2
          CALL FXO$CLOSE ; Close Output File
          JZ   FCERR
          ...


     Thió  simplå examplå illustrateó thå flexibilitù oæ thå 
FXIÏ  routines®   Aó manù fileó aó desireä maù bå  opeî  foò 
inpuô oò output¬  eacè filå havinç itó owî I/Ï Controì Blocë 
anä  Workinç  Buffer®   Thå  advantageó  iî  efficienô  disë 
accessinç  witè thió seô oæ routineó oveò thå previouó  oneó 
are notable.

     Thå  majoò disadvantagå oæ usinç theså routineó ió thaô 
thå  bufferó arå largeò anä thå overheaä oæ alwayó  ensurinç 
thaô  DÅ pointó tï thå propeò I/Ï Controì Blocë beforå  eacè 
routine is called is present.

:FXIO Open Routines
     Routine Names:  FXI$OPEN, FXO$OPEN

     Functionº

     Opeî thå filå whoså I/Ï Controì Blocë ió pointeä tï  bù 
DÅ  foò  Inpuô (FXI$OPEN© oò  Outpuô  (FXO$OPEN)®   FXI$OPEÎ 
